# Galaxies, a cloud port of Stars! Nova.
#
# Deliberately narrow. There is no `* text=auto` here, because adding one would
# renormalize the entire upstream Stars! Nova tree in a single commit and bury the
# port's real history under a whitespace diff. This file only pins the cases where
# a line-ending conversion would cause a bug rather than an annoyance.
#
# The reason this matters: the repository is a Windows OneDrive folder mounted
# over WSL, so the same file can be written with LF by a Linux toolchain and read
# back with CRLF. The committed fixture drifted by exactly six bytes that way, in
# <Description> strings inherited from components.xml.

# ---- Engine data files: byte exact, never converted -------------------------
# M0 exit criterion 4 compares a generated .sstate against a committed golden
# BYTE FOR BYTE, across .NET Framework 4.8 on Windows and net10.0 on Linux. If git
# rewrites line endings on checkout, that comparison fails for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the engine, and the tempting fix is to re-baseline the
# golden, which would mask exactly the cross-architecture divergence the check
# exists to catch. These must round trip untouched.
*.sstate  -text
*.cstate  -text
*.intel   -text
*.orders  -text
*.race    -text
*.settings -text

# components.xml is the input those files inherit description strings from, so it
# has to be as stable as they are.
components.xml -text

# ---- Windows scripts: must keep CRLF ----------------------------------------
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# ---- Shell scripts: must keep LF or they will not run -----------------------
*.sh   text eol=lf

# ---- Binary assets: never diffed, never converted ---------------------------
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.ico  binary
*.xcf  binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.zip  binary
*.7z   binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
